<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carolingian Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Carolingians, Carolingian, Frankish empire, Frankish Empire</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Carolingian Empire was the Frankish realm ruled by the Carolingian dynasty, reaching its height under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>, who was crowned emperor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 800. It covered much of western and central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and fostered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-renaissance">Carolingian Renaissance</a>. Divided by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-verdun">Treaty of Verdun</a> in 843, it was the forerunner of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, and exchanged embassies with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire.jpg" alt="Carolingian Empire" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: maix¿?; derivative work by Alphathon · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Francia_814.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
